# TRACK mobile — development environment.
# Committed on purpose: no secrets (localhost), so a fresh clone runs
# `npx expo start` with zero setup.
#
# Expo loads env files per mode, first match wins (SDK 58):
#   development: .env.development.local > .env.local > .env.development > .env
#   production:  .env.production.local  > .env.local > .env.production  > .env
# This file therefore ONLY affects development builds — a localhost value
# here can never ship inside `expo export` or an EAS release build.
#
# Machine-specific override (emulator / physical device): put
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL in `mobile/.env.local` (gitignored) instead:
#   Android emulator:  http://10.0.2.2:8000/api
#   iOS simulator:     http://localhost:8000/api
#   Physical device:   http://<YOUR-MACHINE-LAN-IP>:8000/api
#     (start Django with DJANGO_EXTRA_ALLOWED_HOSTS=<that IP>)
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
